        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A garage can work, but check the manual first.</strong> Many
            specify indoor, climate-controlled use, and environmental damage may not be covered. If
            you go ahead, the threats are cold, condensation, damp, dust and garage circuits — not
            the garage as such.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Mat, cover, stable temperature, proper outlet, warm-up.</strong>
            Those five deal with most of it. Lubricate and vacuum more often than indoors, and see our
            <a href="/treadmill-maintenance-checklist/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">maintenance checklist</a>
            for how the schedule changes in a garage.
          </p>
